# Everything the build should never see.
#
# The first two lines matter most. Copying a host `node_modules` into the image
# is how a macOS Prisma engine — libquery_engine-darwin-arm64.dylib.node — ends
# up in a Linux container, where it fails at the first query with an error that
# says nothing about architecture. `dist` and `.next` are the same hazard for
# compiled output: stale artefacts that silently win over what the build just
# produced.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Secrets. `.env.example` is deliberately kept — it is documentation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*

.git
.github
**/*.log

# Test and audit output, none of which belongs in a runtime image.
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# Docs and plans: large, and nothing at runtime reads them.
docs
README.md
**/*.md
!package.json
